## 🎯 Attraction Design: Strongman High Striker
A rogue-like carnival strength game where players swing a mallet to launch a puck up a tower, battling variable friction, shifting bells, and sabotaged equipment.

### Declared Handles
  platform (userdata)  The cracked base platform that wobbles and contains shock plates. [owner: Static foundation with wobble sensor, lifecycle: static]
  lever (userdata)  The weighted lever with randomized counter-weight spring tension. [owner: Kinematic fulcrum, lifecycle: static]
  mallet (userdata)  The heavy mallet head that splinters and loses power over time. [owner: Dynamic striker, lifecycle: dynamic]
  puck (userdata)  The puck subject to rusty rails friction and mass variants. [owner: Dynamic projectile, lifecycle: dynamic]
  bell (userdata)  The bell that shifts vertically along the tower track. [owner: Kinematic target, lifecycle: static]
  rusty_rails (userdata)  Variable friction rails affecting puck ascent. [owner: Sensor/Obstacle, lifecycle: static]
  puck_pool (userdata)  Pool for pucks to handle respawn and destruction logic. [owner: Object Pool, lifecycle: managed]

### Module State Variables (declared at module root by the skeleton builder)
  lever_tension (number) = 1.0 - Current spring tension multiplier for the lever. [task init_physics]
  mallet_durability (number) = 100 - Current health of the mallet head before splintering. [task init_physics]
  puck_height (number) = 0 - Current vertical position of the puck on the tower. [task game_loop]
  echo_streak (number) = 0 - Consecutive hits on the same spot for rhythm bonus. [task game_loop]
  shock_timer (number) = 0 - Time remaining before shock plate zaps player. [task game_loop]
  bell_offset (number) = 0 - Current vertical shift of the bell. [task game_loop]
  wager_tokens (number) = 0 - Soul Tokens wagered in current streak. [task economy_calc]
  streak_active (boolean) = False - Flag indicating if the Streak Protocol is currently rolling. [task economy_calc]

### OnLoad Registration Order
  1. SpawnStaticBox(platform)
  2. SpawnKinematicBox(lever)
  3. SpawnDynamicBox(mallet)
  4. SpawnDynamicSphere(puck)
  5. SpawnKinematicBox(bell)
  6. SpawnStaticBox(rusty_rails)
  7. CreatePool(puck_pool, 3, 1)

### Event Flow
  Mallet impact on lever → ApplyImpulse to lever; Reset puck velocity
  Puck hits bell → Check height; Award Tickets; Trigger Streak Protocol
  Shock plate timer expires → ApplyImpulse to player (if standing on platform)
  Mallet durability reaches 0 → Spawn new mallet from hidden room; Destroy old mallet
  Tower Gauge Shift event → DestroyBody(puck); MoveKinematic(bell, new_height); SpawnDynamicSphere(puck, new_height)

### Pool Requirements
  puck_pool: 3

### Economy Hooks: Engine.AwardTickets, Engine.AwardTokens, Engine.GetStreak

### Feature Checklist
  - Rusty Rails variable friction
  - Weighted Puck mass reduction
  - Counter-Weight Springs random tension
  - Bell vertical shifting
  - Cracked Base wobble
  - Echo Strikes rhythm mechanic
  - Sabotaged Mallet durability
  - Shock Plates hazard
  - Tower Gauge Shift respawn

